.TH sam-jail-profile 1 2026-11-23 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail\-profile \- Read or replace the full profile (JSON on stdin for `set`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail profile\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read or replace the full profile (JSON on stdin for `set`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sam\-jail\-profile\-get(1)
Print an app\*(Aqs permissions as JSON
.TP
sam\-jail\-profile\-set(1)
Replace permissions from JSON (a PermissionSet) on stdin
.TP
sam\-jail\-profile\-change(1)
Change permissions: reads {"from": …, "to": …} (two PermissionSets) on stdin and applies only what differs between them, so changes made elsewhere in the meantime stay. A setting changed elsewhere to another value is refused (code changed\-meanwhile)
.TP
sam\-jail\-profile\-reset(1)
Reset to the recommended profile
